  "decision": {
    "classification": "physical max_requests=4 group ceiling with a dominant per-subgroup accept/commit/readback dependency window; direct verifier submit is secondary in host timing",
    "evidence": [
      "Every one of 10 waves per width resolves exactly [1], [3], [4,1], and [4,4] physical request groups at C1/C3/C5/C8; the owner capacity is 8 but capability/partition max_requests is 4 and the workspace is [4,5120].",
      "The EngineLoop executes contiguous subgroups serially inside one scheduler tick. At C8, two size-4 groups therefore pay two complete speculative subcycles before events are returned.",
      "Size-4 timing is invariant from C5 to C8: named stage 146.097->146.340 ms/group-cycle; accept 103.891->103.744 ms and target submit 33.680->33.846 ms. The width deficit is subgroup replication, not slower group-4 arithmetic at C8.",
      "At C8 the two serial groups total 207.488 ms accept out of 292.681 ms named stages (70.9%); selected commit plus blocking readback account for 207.060 ms. The readback timer is a dependency wait that retires queued device work, not pure transfer compute.",
      "Draft acceptance, conditional positional acceptance, and each prompt/request candidate/accepted sequence are identical across C1/C3/C5/C8. Acceptance degradation is excluded.",
      "D1-D24 decode-only MTP/AR falls from 1.722x at C1 and 1.146x at C3 to 0.611x at C5 and 0.603x at C8."
    ],
    "next": "Price widening the physical request/frontier/accept workspace to eight, or issue bounded subgroups before one shared dependency readback. Any implementation needs a RED ownership/lifecycle test, strict fallback, full execution-profile gate, and the complete multi-prompt suite. Rows2-8 verifier sidecar timing can bound a leaf but is not the primary remedy."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The D1/D24 pair is one current-source diagnostic measurement, not a repeated performance promotion and does not replace the canonical C1-C8 score row.",
    "Host timers identify where dependency waits are charged. In particular target_readback_ms includes retirement of queued verifier/accept/commit work and is not device-transfer duration.",
    "Physical groups are reconstructed from exact per-group counters copied to every member row; proposal_physical_rows and the source partition bound independently confirm the sizes.",
    "The unrelated pre-existing untracked scripts/gguf_packed_prefill_grouping_probe.py was present but neither imported nor executed."
  ],
